2-28T13:03:14-08:00","id":1371077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1224144-domus-sanctus-compact?p=1371074#post1371074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ahh ok. so they would likely be the one compact that is unwilling to utilize bygones. last question, what would you say is the prevailing flaw of this compact? like how for Null Mysteriis it's the tendency to test theories out that really should not be tested</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that their main flaw is their faith- they think that they know how mysterious places work, and how they should deal with them. They think that monsters are not the problem and that they should ignore them in favor of purifying places. They truly believe that it is better to let monsters to roam free while spending years cleansing a place. When seeing a Nest, they would seek for whatever supernatural source which spawned the monster to clean it- and if there is none, they would assume that the monster came from somewhere else, and would search for the source- while the monster goes around and kills people.<br /> <br /> So in short, their flaw is that they truly think that they got it all figured out- and as such, they are willing to sacrifice short term victories in price of long term achievements. Maybe they have a point, and perhaps they could indeed &quot;clean&quot; the world from darkness and the monsters would fall apart by themselves. But even if they are right- the Vigil is made of countless small, short term victories. Ignore the monsters for too long, and there will be nothing left to save.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-02-28T16:31:37-08:00","id":1371109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1224144-domus-sanctus-compact?p=1371077#post1371077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that their main flaw is their faith- they think that they know how mysterious places work, and how they should deal with them. They think that monsters are not the problem and that they should ignore them in favor of purifying places. They truly believe that it is better to let monsters to roam free while spending years cleansing a place. When seeing a Nest, they would seek for whatever supernatural source which spawned the monster to clean it- and if there is none, they would assume that the monster came from somewhere else, and would search for the source- while the monster goes around and kills people.<br /> <br /> So in short, their flaw is that they truly think that they got it all figured out- and as such, they are willing to sacrifice short term victories in price of long term achievements. Maybe they have a point, and perhaps they could indeed &amp;quot;clean&amp;quot; the world from darkness and the monsters would fall apart by themselves. But even if they are right- the Vigil is made of countless small, short term victories. Ignore the monsters for too long, and there will be nothing left to save.</div> </div> </div> </div>eloquently put at the end. well I really do like the sound of this compact. I do wonder if them and the Keepers of the Source could have long term alliances. anyway, definitely love the sound of this group, and I hope 2nd edition will inspire more of your home brew hunter Orgs. I really do enjoy reading them.<br /> <br /> also, their flaw being sacrificing the short term for the long term is definitely a breath of fresh air. it's usually always the reverse","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}